dy in my hand), making it nearly impossible to form a useful combination. Discarding B9 preserves maximum flexibility: I keep B7-B8-B8 which can wait for B6 (4 available) to form B6-B7-B8, keep the J2 pair, and maintain B3-B4-B4-B5-B5 which has multiple completion possibilities (B3-B4-B5 chow, B4 or B5 pungs, or B4-B5-B6 chow with 4 B6 tiles available).\n\nAnswer: Play B9"}
