alf Flush potential)\n- If I discard B5: Maintains pairs but wastes the most available tile\n\nReason: \nDiscarding J2 gives me the cleanest path to a winning hand. It keeps my hand focused on Dots tiles only, which allows for \"Half Flush\" (6 points) scoring. I can wait for B3, B5, or B8 to form additional pungs, giving me multiple winning possibilities. With B5 having 4 tiles still unshown and good availability of B3 and B8, this maximizes my winning chances while maintaining high scoring potential through \"All Pungs\" + \"Half Flush\" combinations.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
